Z||000007||Spyder||06-30-2001||05:04 PM||||Some people are using the Honda clear lights, $30.00 for the pair. They don't have the separate inside housings though, and you have to do some bondo work.<BR>The only clear ones that I have seen that are not the real Ferrari are the one on the Fiero Factory 282:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fierofactory.com/f282.jpg"> <BR>I bought the real clear Ferrari ones, Ouch! on the price:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/Myfrontlight.JPG"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Adrift||06-30-2001||05:18 PM||||Here's a real ferrari 355. Notice how it doesn't have clear lights (just food for thought, I personally like the clear turn signals as well)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/01-052right1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>My Dream Fiero, you ask?<BR>That would be a automatic '86 or newer V6 GT Fastback with T-Tops and A/C, fully running and for sale for under $1000 CAN. Know someone who's selling a car like this for this price in the Toronto area? PLEASE E-MAIL ME!!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Spyder||06-30-2001||06:01 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.ferrariturbo.com/Pictures/355Pictureslarge/35545.jpg"> <BR>Go to your local Ferrari Dealership, go to the parts department and order the OEM (Stock) "European" front lights, which are clear. $360.00 US Dollars. That is what I did.||||reg||12
